      "text": [
        " «يَا مُيَسِّرُ تُصَلِّي اَلْعَصْرَ أَرْبَعاً أَفْضَلُ أَوْ تُصَلِّيهَا سِتّاً» فَقُلْتُ أُصَلِّيهَا أَرْبَعاً قَالَ «فَكَذَلِكَ سُنَّةُ رَسُولِ اَللَّهِ صَلَّى اَللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ أَفْضَلُ مِنْ غَيْرِهَا»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2529 - Maysar asked Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) about a man who assumed Ihram from Al-‘Aqiq and another who assumed Ihram from Kufa, saying:\n\"Which of them has performed a better act?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"O Maysar, is it better to pray the afternoon prayer as four units or as six units?\"\nI said: \"To pray it as four units.\"\nImam (as) said: \"Likewise, the practice of the Messenger of Allah (swt) (peace of Allah (swt) be upon him and his family) is better than anything else.\""
        ]
      }
    },
